{
  "meta": {
    "templateCredsSetupCompleted": false
  },
  "name": "Send weekly Slack alerts for new job openings at target accounts",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0001-4c1e-9a01-000000000001",
      "name": "Every Monday 08:00",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                1
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 8
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0007-4c1e-9a01-000000000007",
      "name": "Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "name": "sheetUrl",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/YOUR_SHEET_ID"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "name": "sheetTab",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Accounts"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "name": "slackChannel",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "#hiring-signals"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0002-4c1e-9a01-000000000002",
      "name": "Read target domains",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').item.json.sheetTab }}"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "url",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').item.json.sheetUrl }}"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.5
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0003-4c1e-9a01-000000000003",
      "name": "Build Actor input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const companies = $input.all().map((i) => String(i.json.Domain || '').trim()).filter(Boolean);\nreturn [{ json: { companies, watchMode: true } }];"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0004-4c1e-9a01-000000000004",
      "name": "Get hiring signals from Apify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        880,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.apify.com/v2/acts/vicarious_film~company-hiring-signals/run-sync-get-dataset-items",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 300000
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0005-4c1e-9a01-000000000005",
      "name": "Opened new roles?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        1100,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "gt"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ ($json.newRoles || []).length }}",
              "rightValue": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0006-4c1e-9a01-000000000006",
      "name": "Post to Slack",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "position": [
        1320,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "={{ $json.input }} opened {{ $json.newRoles.length }} role(s) this week ({{ $json.openRoles }} open, velocity {{ $json.hiringVelocity }}): {{ $json.newRoles.slice(0, 5).map(r => r.title).join(', ') }}{{ $json.signals.includes('hiring_sales') ? ' \u00b7 hiring in sales' : '' }}",
        "select": "channel",
        "channelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "={{ $('Settings').item.json.slackChannel }}"
        },
        "otherOptions": {}
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0101-4c1e-9a01-000000000101",
      "name": "About this template",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Send weekly Slack alerts when target accounts open new jobs\n\n**Who's it for:** sales, SDR and growth teams who use hiring as a buying signal (\"they're hiring 3 SDRs, they need our tool\") and want a weekly nudge instead of checking careers pages by hand.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Every Monday it reads your target company domains from a Google Sheet.\n2. It sends them to the [Company Hiring Signals](https://apify.com/vicarious_film/company-hiring-signals) Apify Actor in watch mode. The Actor finds each company's job board (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby or Workable) from the bare domain and compares it with last week.\n3. For each company that opened roles, it posts one Slack message: how many new roles, their titles, total open roles, hiring velocity, and a note when they're hiring in sales.\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Put your domains in a sheet with a column named `Domain`.\n2. In **Settings**, paste your sheet URL and Slack channel.\n3. Add an Apify API token as a Header Auth credential (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`) on the Apify node.\n4. Connect Google Sheets and Slack, then run once. The first run records the baseline; alerts start the following week.\n\n**Requirements:** Google Sheets, Slack, and an Apify account (free plan works). About $0.006 per company with a job board found; companies without one are free.\n\n**How to customize:** change the schedule, filter on `signals` (for example `hiring_engineering`), or send email instead of Slack."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0102-4c1e-9a01-000000000102",
      "name": "Step 1 \u2013 settings and list",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        180,
        -200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 160,
        "content": "### 1. Settings and your list\nSet your sheet URL, tab and Slack channel in **Settings**. The sheet needs a `Domain` column (ramp.com, gitlab.com, \u2026)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0103-4c1e-9a01-000000000103",
      "name": "Step 2 \u2013 hiring signals",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        -200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 160,
        "content": "### 2. Hiring signals (watch mode)\nOne row per company: ATS, open roles, new roles since the last run, velocity and signals like `hiring_sales`. Credential: Header Auth `Authorization: Bearer <Apify token>`."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b1a1f0a0-0104-4c1e-9a01-000000000104",
      "name": "Step 3 \u2013 alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1060,
        -200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 160,
        "content": "### 3. Alert on new roles\nOnly companies that opened roles since last week are posted to Slack."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
